@page
@model woodgrovedemo.Help.Pages.SmsAuthenticationModel

@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "SMS authentication";
    Layout = "_Layout";
}

<h1 style="margin-top: 25px; margin-bottom: 25px;">Enable SMS authentication</h1>

<p>
    Microsoft Entra External ID can send a one-time passcode by text message (SMS)
    as an authentication method — for example, as a second factor for
    sign-in/MFA. This demo's deployment automation enables the SMS authentication
    method and provisions a dedicated group so you can opt users in, but two
    prerequisites can't be automated via Microsoft Graph and must be completed by
    hand.
</p>

<div class="alert alert-warning" role="alert">
    <h4 class="alert-heading">SMS is a paid, pay-as-you-go feature</h4>
    <p class="mb-0">
        Unlike Email OTP (used for self-service password reset, included in base
        billing), SMS/voice authentication is billed per-message on a
        pay-as-you-go basis. Before SMS can be used, the Entra External ID (CIAM)
        tenant must be linked to an Azure subscription with billing enabled.
    </p>
</div>

@await Html.PartialAsync("_HelpSelector.cshtml", 1)
<div class="tab-content wg-tab-content">
    <div class="tab-pane active" id="microsoftEntraAdminCenter" role="tabpanel"
        aria-labelledby="microsoftEntraAdminCenter-tab" tabindex="0">

        @await Html.PartialAsync("_StepsButtons.cshtml")

        <div class="bs-stepper vertical" id="Stepper">
            @await Html.PartialAsync("_Steps.cshtml", 4)

            <div class="bs-stepper-content">
                <div id="step-1" role="tabpanel" class="bs-stepper-pane fade active" aria-labelledby="steppertrigger1">
                    @await Html.PartialAsync("_Prerequisites.cshtml")

                    <h4>Link the tenant to an Azure subscription for billing</h4>
                    <p>
                        Sign in to the <a href="https://entra.microsoft.com/" target="_blank"
                            class="link-dark link-offset-2">Microsoft Entra admin center</a> for your
                        External ID (CIAM) tenant. Browse to your tenant's overview page and confirm
                        (or link) an associated Azure subscription with billing enabled — this is
                        required before SMS can be used, regardless of how the authentication method
                        itself is configured.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div id="step-2" role="tabpanel" class="bs-stepper-pane fade" aria-labelledby="steppertrigger2">
                    <h4>Confirm SMS is enabled in Authentication methods</h4>
                    <p>
                        This demo's deployment pipeline (<code>deploy-infra.yml</code>) automatically
                        enables the SMS authentication method for a dedicated group named
                        <b>Woodgrove SMS Authentication</b>, by calling Microsoft Graph:
                    </p>
                    <code style="color: black;">PATCH https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/policies/authenticationMethodsPolicy/authenticationMethodConfigurations/sms</code>
                    <p class="mt-3">
                        You can confirm this took effect by browsing to
                        <b>Identity</b> &gt; <b>Protection</b> &gt; <b>Authentication methods</b> &gt;
                        <b>Policies</b> &gt; <b>SMS</b> and checking that the
                        <b>Woodgrove SMS Authentication</b> group is listed under <b>Include</b>.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        If the deployer identity used by the pipeline lacked the
                        <code>Policy.ReadWrite.AuthenticationMethod</code> Graph permission, or the
                        tenant wasn't yet linked to a subscription (step 1), this step logs a warning
                        and continues rather than failing the deployment — you can enable SMS manually
                        here instead.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div id="step-3" role="tabpanel" class="bs-stepper-pane fade" aria-labelledby="steppertrigger3">
                    <h4>Add users to the SMS authentication group</h4>
                    <p>
                        Unlike Email OTP, the SMS authentication method's target does <b>not</b>
                        support a synthetic "all users" option — Microsoft Graph only accepts a real
                        group object ID. This means SMS is opt-in by design: no user is enrolled by
                        default.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Browse to <b>Identity</b> &gt; <b>Groups</b> &gt; <b>All groups</b>, select
                        <b>Woodgrove SMS Authentication</b>, then <b>Members</b> &gt; <b>Add members</b>
                        to opt a test user in.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div id="step-4" role="tabpanel" class="bs-stepper-pane fade" aria-labelledby="steppertrigger4">
                    <h4>Add a phone number to the test user</h4>
                    <p>
                        The opted-in user needs a registered phone authentication method before SMS
                        sign-in/verification will work. Browse to <b>Identity</b> &gt; <b>Users</b>,
                        select the test user, then <b>Authentication methods</b> &gt;
                        <b>Add authentication method</b> &gt; <b>Phone</b>, and enter a mobile number.
                    </p>

                    <div class="alert alert-success" role="alert">
                        <h4 class="alert-heading">Well done!</h4>
                        <p class="mb-0">
                            The user can now use SMS as an authentication method where your user flow
                            or Conditional Access policy allows it.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

    </div>

    <div class="tab-pane" id="microsoftGraph" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="microsoftGraph-tab" tabindex="0">

        <h4 class="graph-header graph-header-space">Enable SMS authentication method for a group</h4>

        <p>
            The following Graph call enables the SMS authentication method for a specific
            group (used by this repo's deployment automation instead of an "all users" target,
            which the SMS authentication method configuration does not support).
        </p>

        <code
            style="color: black;">PATCH https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/policies/authenticationMethodsPolicy/authenticationMethodConfigurations/sms</code>

        <pre>
{
    "state": "enabled",
    "excludeTargets": [],
    "includeTargets": [
        {
            "targetType": "group",
            "id": "&lt;woodgrove-sms-authentication-group-object-id&gt;",
            "isUsableForSignIn": false
        }
    ]
}
        </pre>
    </div>

    <div class="tab-pane" id="entraGraphPowerShell" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="entraGraphPowerShell-tab"
        tabindex="0">
        Loading...
    </div>
</div>
